  "summary": "Designed for effortless entertaining and busy weeknight prep, this <b>Korean roasted pork belly</b> relies on a deep overnight marinade to deliver maximum flavor with minimal same-day effort. Strips of savory pork belly soak up a balanced mixture of savory soy sauce, spicy gochujang chili paste, sweet brown sugar, and tangy pear juice that tenderizes the meat while infusing intense savoriness. Sliced ginger and crushed garlic add vibrant sharp notes that cut cleanly through the rich profile of the pork belly. When ready to cook, high-heat roasting in the oven renders the marbled fat into crispy edges while keeping the interior juicy and tender. As the natural sugars caramelize on the hot pan, they create a sticky glaze that clings beautifully to every piece. Preparing this dish ahead allows the flavors to mature fully inside the refrigerator before baking. Serve these glazed pork belly strips sliced alongside steamed rice, pickled radish, and fresh lettuce wraps for an customizable meal that tastes like it took hours of active preparation.",
